<title>PHILIPPINES: Singapore brokerage seeks seat at Manila bourse.</title>
<headline>Singapore brokerage seeks seat at Manila bourse.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Securities 2000 Inc, a brokerage house from Singapore, has sought the Philippine Stock Exchange's approval for a broker's seat it bought from a local company, bourse officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Rafael Llave, the bourse's chief operating officer, said Securities 2000 Inc is owned by Singapore Tecnologies Pte Ltd, a technology-based multinational conglomerate wholly-owned by the government of Singapore through its investment arm Temasek Holdings.</p>
<p>The brokerage house bought an existing seat held by Anthony Dee Chiong for 70 million pesos, officials said.</p>
<p>The exchange has 185 memberships, of which 179 are active.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
